# QRWare API Test File
# This file can be used with VS Code REST Client extension or IntelliJ HTTP Client
# Copy and paste these requests into your preferred HTTP client

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================
### 1. HEALTH & STATUS CHECKS (Public)
### ============================================

### Basic Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Detailed Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/status

### Database Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health/database

### Ping
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ping

### Version Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/version

### Environment Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/environment

### Readiness Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ready

### Liveness Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/live

### ============================================
### 2. TEST ENDPOINTS (Public)
### ============================================

### Public Test Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/public

### CORS Test
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/cors

### System Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/system-info

### ============================================
### 3. AUTHENTICATION (Public)
### ============================================

### Register New User
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "TestPass123!",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "phone": "+48123456789"
}

###

### Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "testuser",
  "password": "TestPass123!"
}

###

### Register Admin User (for testing admin endpoints)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "admin",
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "AdminPass123!",
  "firstName": "Admin",
  "lastName": "User"
}

###

### Login as Admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "admin",
  "password": "AdminPass123!"
}

###

### Check Username Availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/check-username?username=newuser

###

### Check Email Availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/check-email?email=new@example.com

###

### Request Password Reset
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

### ============================================
### 4. PROTECTED ENDPOINTS (Require Token)
### ============================================
### Note: Replace YOUR_JWT_TOKEN with actual token from login response

@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN

### Get Current User Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Validate Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Protected Test Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/protected
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Token Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/token-info
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Permission Test
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Warehouse Test Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/warehouse
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Manager Test Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/manager
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Admin Test Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Echo Test (POST)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/test/echo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "message": "Hello QRWare!",
  "timestamp": "2024-01-01T10:00:00",
  "testData": {
    "key1": "value1",
    "key2": 123,
    "key3": true
  }
}

###

### Change Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "currentPassword": "TestPass123!",
  "newPassword": "NewTestPass123!"
}

###

### Refresh Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refreshToken": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN"
}

###

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 5. ERROR TESTING
### ============================================

### Test Error Handling
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/error

###

### Test Unauthorized Access
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/unauthorized
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Test Invalid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/protected
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here

###

### Test Missing Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/protected

### ============================================
### 6. ACTUATOR ENDPOINTS (Some require admin)
### ============================================

### Health Actuator
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

###

### Info Actuator
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/info

###

### Metrics Actuator (Admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 7. QUICK TEST SEQUENCE
### ============================================

### 1. Check if system is running
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### 2. Test public endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/public

### 3. Register user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "quicktest",
  "email": "quicktest@example.com",
  "password": "QuickTest123!",
  "firstName": "Quick",
  "lastName": "Test"
}

### 4. Login and get token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "quicktest",
  "password": "QuickTest123!"
}

### 5. Test protected endpoint (use token from step 4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test/protected
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
